WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:06.370
Have you ever watched fireflies
flashing on a humid summer evening? Or

2
00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:10.880
have you swum on a warm summer night
and been surrounded by green flashes?

3
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:16.450
This is the phenomenon of
bioluminescence, the production of

4
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.640
light by living organisms. These
flashes of light can have many

5
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.180
purposes, from hunting prey, to evading
predators, to attracting mates.

6
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:30.660
Bioluminescence produces bright light
without making toxic byproducts or

7
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.990
excessive heat, either of which could
be dangerous. To do this, chemical

8
00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:41.160
reactions are controlled by proteins
called enzymes. For example, fireflies

9
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.860
have an enzyme called luciferase that
converts the chemical luciferin to

10
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:52.470
oxyluciferin. This reaction also uses
ATP and oxygen and creates diphosphate,

11
00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.710
AMP, carbon dioxide, and light.

12
00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:01.340
Bioluminescence is really important in
biomedical research because it is

13
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:05.750
possible to take the luciferase gene
from fireflies and transfer it to other

14
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.360
cells. Those cells then produce the
luciferase protein and will make light

15
00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:14.960
when exposed to luciferin. Scientists
have taken advantage of luciferase to

16
00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.470
create reporter assays that help them
track gene activity, such that cells

17
00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.940
produce light only when the gene of
interest is turned on, or as a way to

18
00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.720
keep track of cells moving through
tissues and models of cancer.

19
00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:34.910
Here, only the cancer cells have the
luciferase gene, and so by watching

20
00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:38.900
where the light goes, we can visualize
them metastasizing through tissues.

21
00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:45.020
Bioluminescence is a mesmerizing
biological phenomenon. Next time you

22
00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.830
sit on the porch and spy a firefly
floating by, remember that these little

23
00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.180
lightning bugs are helping scientists
to understand the world and to cure

24
00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:52.820
cancer.

